and consideration of pathogenesis</article-title><source>Am J Clin Pathol</source><year>1980</year><volume>73</volume><fpage>740</fpage><lpage>747</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7395802</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b6-0100055"><label>6</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Parfrey</surname><given-names>PS</given-names></name><name><surname>Bear</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Morgan</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The diagnosis and prognosis of autosomal dominant polycystic kidney disease</article-title><source>N Engl J Med</source><year>1990</year><volume>323</volume><fpage>1085</fpage><lpage>1090</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2215575</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b7-0100055"><label>7</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Langdorf</surname><given-names>MI</given-names></name><name><surname>Rudkin</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Dellota</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Fox</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name><name><surname>Munden</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Decision rule and utility of routine urine toxicology screening of trauma patients</article-title><source>Eur J Emerg Med</source><year>2002</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>121</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12131632</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b8-0100055"><label>8</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grantham</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Torres</surname><given-names>VE</given-names></name><name><surname>Chapman</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name></person-group><collab>CRISP Investigators</collab><article-title>Volume progression in poly